Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||08-24-99||11:35 AM||||Thanks for all the great feedback!<p>Batboy, thanks! <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>Formula, thanks! yes.. That's one of the first links I put in. Currently they're ordered from commercial sites to personal sites to modifications.. The mods are going to be moving to a separate page soon tho, as are the links and photos.. See the menu posted above for the different sections.<p>FieroGT, That'd be perfect for the modifications section. Thanks!<p>Chad, thanks.. I was looking at some other kits for a while, as the Finale ones on PISA didn't look like what I wanted. Then I found a couple other places selling Finales, and they had much better pictures.. So that's definitely the kit I plan on getting. I also want a turbocharged V8, porsche suspension, etc.. so it might be a while. <IMG SRC="/ubb/wink.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
Z||000013||FieroGT||08-24-99||12:12 PM||||ChadMan:<br>
Z||000014||FieroGT||08-24-99||12:22 PM||||ChadMan:    Oops! Hit enter by mistake! Yes, those are my seats at the bottom of DaRkLoRd's page. I think I got lucky with the price, because I only paid $150 for both of them, including the wiring harness, nuts/bolts, and bolt caps. Your results will vary greatly. I had a guy from California tell me that he was quoted $300 per seat!                                               It wasn't perfect, though. After completing the wiring, I found out that the driver's side left bolster would inflate, and slowly deflate. I tracked the leak down to the inflatable air bladder. Turns out that it doesn't take too much effort to replace them. The seatbacks are screwed to the seat assembly, and are easily removed for such occassions. There was even a part number on the bladder! So on Friday, I'll be getting a new on from my friendly GM dealer for $23.00. I guess no project is complete until you run into some kind of problem. My personal motto: If the job went perfectly, you probably screwed something up. Good luck if you decide to hunt for seats!
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||08-24-99||12:53 PM||||FieroGT, Let me know when you get that written up, I'll add it to the Mods section of my site.<p>Dan, Thanks for the pics, would you be able to provide a short description of the GTFX conversion? I could try to put captions under the pics, but I know I'd make a few mistakes. I'd only be guessing what was going in in some of the steps.<p>I've changed the URL of my site to reflect that it's now a Fiero page.. Batboy, and anyone else who's linked to it, the new URL is:<br> <A HREF="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/fiero/</A> 
